            <h2>Train Duration, Distance, and Travel Time Overview</h2>
            <p>
                Traveling from Baltimore to Boston covers roughly 359 miles (578 km) along the busy Northeast Corridor, linking two of the East Coast’s most historic cities. Although this isn’t a high‑speed rail corridor like in Europe, Amtrak’s Acela and Northeast Regional trains offer a steady and pleasant pace, often making the trip more enjoyable than a long drive.
