            <h3>High-Speed vs Regional Trains</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>The Acela is Amtrak’s flagship high-speed service, offering speeds up to 82.2 mph (with NextGen trains reaching 160 mph in some sections), making it the fastest option on this route.</li>
                <li>Northeast Regional is considered a regional/intercity train with consistent speeds and predictable travel times, serving more stops along the corridor.</li>
                <li>While slower than flying, both services offer comfortable seating, scenic views, and city-center arrivals, which can save time compared to driving during heavy traffic.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Travel is steady, reliable, and scenic, with Acela offering a premium high-speed experience.</li>
                <li>The lack of transfers on most services simplifies planning, especially for first-time rail travelers.</li>
                <li>Choosing the train over driving allows relaxation, work, or sightseeing during the trip, with Acela providing significant time savings.</li>
            </ul>
