                <li><b>Class Selection:</b> Coach is the budget-friendly option, while Business Class and Acela provide extra amenities at higher prices.</li>
                <li><b>Time of Travel:</b> Weekend departures, holidays, or trains during popular hours may have higher fares.</li>
                <li><b>Demand &amp; Availability: </b>The busy Northeast Corridor means prices fluctuate with train capacity and seasonal demand.</li>
                <li><b>Service Type:</b> Acela commands a premium over Northeast Regional due to speed and luxury amenities.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Budget travelers should book early and consider the Northeast Regional Coach for the best value.</li>
                <li>Business travelers may find Acela Business or First Class worth the premium for time savings and productivity.</li>
