            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from Baltimore to Boston?</h3>
            <p>The train journey typically takes 6 to 8 hours on the Northeast Regional, or approximately 5 hours 59 minutes on the fastest Acela service.</p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from Baltimore to Boston?</h3>
            <p>The fastest option is Amtrak Acela, which can complete the journey in approximately 5 hours and 59 minutes with direct service.</p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from Baltimore to Boston cost?</h3>
            <p>Ticket prices generally fall between:</p>
            <p><b>$49-$80 for early booking on the Northeast Regional Coach</b></p>
            <p><b>$80-$120 for standard Northeast Regional fares</b></p>
            <p><b>$100-$180 for Northeast Regional Business</b></p>
            <p><b>$150-$350+ for Acela Business</b></p>
            <p><b>$250-$500+ for Acela First or last-minute travel</b></p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from Baltimore to Boston?</h3>
            <p>Yes, most Amtrak Northeast Regional and Acela trains are direct, so there’s no need for transfers.</p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard?</h3>
            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café car, and luggage space. Acela adds premium seating, at-seat meal service (First Class), and priority boarding.</p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving?</h3>
            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 6-8 hours, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and allows productive travel time.</p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from Baltimore to Boston in one day?</h3>
            <p>Yes, the route is suitable for same-day trips, but early departures are recommended to maximize time in Boston.</p>

            <h3>8. Which station in Baltimore do trains depart from?</h3>
            <p>Most trains depart from Baltimore Penn Station, located in downtown Baltimore. Some connections are available from BWI Airport Station.</p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Boston?</h3>
            <p>Trains arrive at Boston South Station, conveniently located in the city center and easily accessible by MBTA Red Line, Silver Line, and other public transport.</p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class or Acela worth it?</h3>
            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom and a quieter environment. At the same time, Acela provides the fastest journey with premium amenities, making both ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 6-8 hour journey.</p>















